==English==

===Etymology===
From the {{calque|en|de|Rheinland|notext=1}}, equivalent to {{cog|en|-}} {{suffix|en|Rhine|land}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{wikipedia}}
{{swp|Rhineland (disambiguation)}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹaɪnlænd/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹaɪnlænd/|a=GA}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|usually|with the {{l|en|definite article}}}} {{place|en|area|on both sides of the river|river/Rhine|in the west of|c/Germany|a=An}}. Roughly equivalent to the former [[Prussian]] {{w|Rhine Province}}, now the greater part of [[Rhineland-Palatinate]] plus the south-western half of [[North Rhine-Westphalia]].
# {{lb|en|uncommon}} All of Germany's territories on the Rhine.
# {{place|en|village|co/Montgomery County|s/Missouri|c/USA}}.
# {{place|en|unincorporated community|co/Knox County|s/Texas|c/USA}}.
# {{place|en|rural municipality|in southern|p/Manitoba|c/Canada}}.
# {{place|en|hamlet|co/Norfolk County|p/Ontario|c/Canada}}.

